CAT = "cpabarGovReporting"; SEG = "GVR"
Q = [
("A county's pension trust fund and its custodial funds are reported in its government-wide financial statements:",
 "Not at all", ["In governmental activities", "In business-type activities", "As component units"],
 "GASB Statement 34 excludes fiduciary activities from the government-wide statements because those resources cannot support the government's own programs. They appear in the fiduciary fund statements."),
("In a city's government-wide statement of activities, which is reported as a general revenue?",
 "Property taxes", ["Charges for services", "Operating grants", "Capital grants"],
 "Program revenues are charges for services and grants and contributions tied to a function. Taxes, even if levied for a specific purpose, are general revenues."),
("Total governmental fund revenues are $50,000,000 and governmental plus enterprise fund revenues are $80,000,000. A special revenue fund has revenues of $5,500,000. The fund is:",
 "Major, meeting both tests", ["Not major, failing the 5% test", "Not major, failing the 10% test", "Major only by election"],
 "The fund's revenues are 11% of the governmental total and 6.9% of the combined total, so it passes the 10% and 5% tests and is a major fund."),
("Which governmental fund is always reported as a major fund?",
 "The general fund", ["The debt service fund", "The largest capital projects fund", "The largest special revenue fund"],
 "GASB Statement 34 requires the general fund to be reported as major. Other funds are major when they meet the 10% and 5% tests or when officials choose."),
("Internal service funds that mainly serve governmental departments are usually reported in the government-wide statements within:",
 "Governmental activities", ["Business-type activities", "A separate fund column", "Fiduciary activities"],
 "Internal service fund balances are generally folded into governmental activities in the government-wide statements, even though they are proprietary funds."),
("In a water utility enterprise fund's statement of cash flows, interest paid on bonds issued to build a treatment plant is classified as:",
 "Capital and related financing", ["Noncapital financing", "Operating activities", "Investing activities"],
 "GASB's proprietary cash flow statement has four categories, and debt for acquiring or building capital assets belongs in capital and related financing activities."),
("Under GASB Statement 103, the proprietary fund statement of revenues, expenses and changes in fund net position must show a subtotal for:",
 "Operating income and noncapital subsidies", ["Income before depreciation", "Revenue net of transfers", "Program revenues by function"],
 "Statement 103 adds a subtotal for operating income (loss) and noncapital subsidies before other nonoperating revenues and expenses are reported."),
("Under GASB Statement 103, budgetary comparison information for the general fund is presented as:",
 "Required supplementary information", ["A basic financial statement", "A note to the statements", "Optional supplementary data"],
 "Statement 103 requires a single method, RSI, with variances between original and final budget and between final budget and actual."),
("Under GASB Statement 103, MD&A must be limited to five sections. Which is one of them?",
 "Financial Summary", ["Statistical Section", "Auditor's Opinion", "Transmittal Letter"],
 "The five sections are Overview of the Financial Statements, Financial Summary, Detailed Analyses, Significant Capital Asset and Long-Term Financing Activity, and Currently Known Facts, Decisions, or Conditions."),
("Under GASB Statement 103, the detailed analyses in MD&A should explain:",
 "Why balances and results changed", ["Only the dollar amounts of change", "Budget rules for the next year", "The auditor's materiality level"],
 "Statement 103 stresses that detailed analyses explain the reasons balances and results of operations changed, not just the amounts or percentages."),
("A component unit is blended into the primary government's funds, rather than presented discretely, when:",
 "Its board is substantively the same", ["It has its own audited statements", "It is a separate legal entity", "Its revenues exceed 10%"],
 "GASB Statement 61 requires blending when the component unit's governing body is substantively the same as the primary government's, among other conditions."),
("A primary government is financially accountable for a legally separate organization when it appoints a voting majority of the organization's board and:",
 "Can impose its will on it", ["Shares a bank account with it", "Audits its statements", "Is located in the same county"],
 "Financial accountability also exists when the primary government appoints the majority and there is a potential financial benefit or burden relationship."),
("Which is required supplementary information other than MD&A for a state that provides defined benefit pensions?",
 "Ten-year pension schedules", ["A statistical section", "A schedule of fund transfers", "A capital asset roll-forward"],
 "GASB Statement 68 requires 10-year schedules, including changes in the net pension liability and contributions, as RSI."),
("Total governmental fund balances are $12,400,000. Capital assets, net, are $58,000,000, bonds payable $31,000,000 and compensated absences $1,200,000. Revenue deferred as unavailable in the funds is $600,000. Net position of governmental activities is:",
 "$38,800,000", ["$38,200,000", "$40,000,000", "$39,400,000"],
 "Reconciling to net position: $12,400,000 + $58,000,000 - $31,000,000 - $1,200,000 + $600,000 of unavailable revenue that is recognized on the accrual basis = $38,800,000.",
 12400000 + 58000000 - 31000000 - 1200000 + 600000),
("The net change in governmental fund balances is $900,000. Capital outlay was $4,000,000, depreciation $2,500,000, bond proceeds $3,000,000 and bond principal repaid $1,000,000. The change in net position of governmental activities is:",
 "$400,000", ["$900,000", "$2,400,000", "$6,400,000"],
 "Adjust the fund change: + $4,000,000 capital outlay - $2,500,000 depreciation - $3,000,000 bond proceeds + $1,000,000 principal repaid, so $900,000 becomes $400,000.",
 900000 + 4000000 - 2500000 - 3000000 + 1000000),
("Under GASB Statement 103, inflows and outflows from an unusual or infrequent item are displayed:",
 "Separately, as the last flows", ["Netted with general revenues", "Only in the notes", "As a special item in equity"],
 "Each unusual or infrequent item is shown separately as the last flow before the net change in resource flows in the government-wide, governmental fund and proprietary fund statements."),
]
